OL,2,V55555555C#20m TREASURE SHIP
OL,3,Vu5u5u5u5CFOUND IN CHANNEL
OL,5, Sunken treasure said to be worth #20m
OL,6, has been found in a 70-year-old wreck
OL,7, off the south Devon coast.
OL,9, The 12,000-ton P&O steamship Medina
OL,10, went down off Start Point in 1917 after
OL,11, being hit by a German torpedo on her
OL,12, return from India loaded with treasure.
OL,14, Her cargo included gifts to the Royal
OL,15, family from Indian rulers and treasures
OL,16, owned by the British Governor, Lord
OL,17, Carmichael Munro.
OL,19, Danish divers located the baggage room
OL,20, where the valuables are stored and have
OL,21, already brought up a Freemason's chain,
OL,22, worth more than #450,000.
OL,23,F]DFrom 18-03-87 / teletextarchive.com
